static const char __pyx_k_solvers_py_Core_solver_function[] = "\nsolvers.py\n\nCore solver functions for DCP (Dark Channel Prior) blind deconvolution.\n\nPorted from MATLAB code by Jinshan Pan (CVPR 2016).\nReference:\n    J. Pan, D. Sun, H. Pfister, M.-H. Yang: \"Blind Image Deblurring\n    Using Dark Channel Prior\", CVPR 2016.\n\nContains:\n    estimate_psf           \342\200\224 PSF estimation via conjugate gradient (estimate_psf.m)\n    L0Deblur_dark_channel  \342\200\224 L0 deblurring with dark-channel + gradient priors\n                             (L0Deblur_dark_chanel.m)\n    L0Restoration          \342\200\224 L0 deblurring with gradient prior only\n                             (L0Restoration.m)\n    blind_deconv_main      \342\200\224 single-scale blind deconvolution loop\n                             (blind_deconv_main.m)\n    blind_deconv           \342\200\224 multi-scale coarse-to-fine blind deconvolution\n                             (blind_deconv.m)\n    deblurring_adm_aniso   \342\200\224 TV-\342\204\223\302\262 deblurring via ADM / Split Bregman\n                             (deblurring_adm_aniso.m)\n    ringing_artifacts_removal \342\200\224 artifact removal post-processing\n                             (ringing_artifacts_removal.m)\n\nMATLAB \342\206\222 Python notes:\n    - MATLAB conv2(A,B,'valid') \342\206\222 scipy.signal.convolve2d(A,B,'valid')\n      Both do true convolution (kernel flip).\n    - MATLAB diff(S,1,2) \342\206\222 np.diff(S, n=1, axis=1)\n      MATLAB dim 2 = Python axis 1 (columns).\n      MATLAB diff(S,1,1) \342\206\222 np.diff(S, n=1, axis=0).\n    - MATLAB S(:,1,:)-S(:,end,:) \342\206\222 S[:,0,:]-S[:,-1,:]\n    - MATLAB repmat(A,[1,1,D]) \342\206\222 np.tile(A, (1,1,D)) or np.broadcast_to\n    - MATLAB fft2/ifft2/conj \342\206\222 np.fft.fft2/ifft2/conj\n    - MATLAB bwconncomp(k,8) \342\206\222 scipy.ndimage.label(k, structure=np.ones((3,3)))\n    - MATLAB imresize(k,ret) \342\206\222 scipy.ndimage.zoom (or cv2.resize)\n    - MATLAB interp2(I,gx,gy,'bilinear') \342\206\222 scipy.nd""image.map_coordinates\n";
